01:02:04.820 --> 01:02:07.780
Baseball, for me, growing up, was a huge thing.

01:02:07.780 --> 01:02:09.780
You know, Hayden wanted to go to baseball camp.

01:02:09.780 --> 01:02:10.980
We got him all the gear.

01:02:10.980 --> 01:02:13.900
As a father, I'm, like, massively, you know,

01:02:13.900 --> 01:02:17.780
prideful and went to coach the team and all that stuff.

01:02:18.740 --> 01:02:19.820
And then the next year, it's like,

01:02:19.820 --> 01:02:22.340
I don't wanna do baseball this year.

01:02:22.340 --> 01:02:23.180
And does it hurt?

01:02:23.180 --> 01:02:24.260
Of course, it's like, what?

01:02:24.260 --> 01:02:26.340
Baseball, you were, it was so good.

01:02:26.340 --> 01:02:28.400
I was coaching and, you know.

01:02:28.400 --> 01:02:32.820
But for me to put my childhood, you know,

01:02:32.820 --> 01:02:36.060
dreams and aspirations and what I really enjoyed

01:02:36.060 --> 01:02:39.860
and put that on him isn't right, it's not right.

01:02:39.900 --> 01:02:42.020
It's not the thing to do.

01:02:42.020 --> 01:02:45.940
And so, now he's going swimming, you know?

01:02:45.940 --> 01:02:50.940
